{
  "Content next to the element it belongs to: a title, a close button, a form, a card. It opens on a press or while the pointer rests on its target, follows it, and points at it with an arrow where the design language has one.": "",
  "The JSX children are the content; `target` names the element or component it opens next to. Programmatically, `content` gives the content and `open()`, `close()` and `toggle()` move it; `value` and `x-model` say whether it is open.": "",
  "While the pointer rests": "",
  "`showOn: 'hover'` opens it after `delay` while the pointer rests on the target, and when the target has keyboard focus; the pointer may move onto the popover. It closes `hideDelay` after the pointer leaves both.": "",
  "Placements, the arrow and a width": "",
  "Keeping it open": "",
  "By a press on the target, by the pointer resting on it (`hover`), or programmatically. It appears in the browser’s top layer, next to the target, and follows it while the page scrolls.": "",
  "Opened by a press or programmatically, focus moves to the first focusable part inside, else to the popover; it goes back to the target when the popover closes. Opened by hover, focus stays where it is.": "",
  "Escape, a press outside it and its target, focus leaving both (Tab out), the close button, the target pressed again, or the pointer leaving both (`hover`). `onClosing` may keep it open.": "",
  "`placement` names the side and the alignment, as for the kit’s popups; without room on that side it opens on the other.": "",
  "Made programmatically, it goes into the nearest container of its target that can hold it, so it stays in the target’s window and landmark.": "",
  "`dialog`, named by its title, else by `label`: give it one.": "",
  "`aria-controls` and `aria-expanded`; `aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"` when a press opens it.": "",
  "Tab moves through the content and out (which closes it); Escape closes and returns focus. A `hover` popover opens on keyboard focus too.": "",
  "Decorative.": "",
  "The popover. `data-side` (`top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end`), `data-arrow`.": "",
  "The arrow.": "",
  "The header, its title and the close button.": "",
  "The content.": "",
  "Units: the surface (`focus`), the arrow (`display`, `size`, its fill and frame), the header, the title and the body.": "",
  "Place: the close button’s look (`variant`).": "",
  "The gap to the target, how far it comes in as it appears, the space between title and close button.": "",
  "The element or component it opens next to.": "",
  "A title in the header. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "What screen readers call it when it has no title.": "",
